::ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q01::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
If f(x)=x^2+1 and g(x)=2x+1, which statement is true at x=3?
{
= f(3)>g(3)#Correct. f(3)=10 and g(3)=7, so f(3) is greater.
~ f(3)<g(3)#This reverses the comparison.
~ f(3)=g(3)#The values are not equal.
~ Both values are 3#The input is 3, but the outputs must be evaluated.
}

::ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q02::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
Solve f(x)=g(x) for f(x)=x^2 and g(x)=4x.
{
~ x=4 only#This misses x=0.
= x=0 and x=4#Correct. x^2=4x gives x(x-4)=0.
~ x=-4 and x=0#The sign on 4 is wrong.
~ x=2#This is not a solution of x^2=4x.
}

::ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q03::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
What is the average rate of change of h(x)=3x+2 from x=1 to x=5?
{
~ 12#This is the change in output, not divided by the input change.
~ 4#This uses the interval length only.
= 3#Correct. (17-5)/(5-1)=12/4=3.
~ 5#This is h(1), not the average rate.
}

::ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q04::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
A model gives t=-2 and t=6 for time in seconds. Which solution is viable?
{
~ t=-2 only#Negative time is not viable in this context.
~ Both solutions#The negative time value must be rejected.
~ Neither solution#The positive time value is viable.
= t=6 only#Correct. Time after the start must be nonnegative.
}

::ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q05::
Question ID: ALG2_U05_L07_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.A2.FN.3; MLA.A2.FN.11; MLA.A2.FN.12
Question:
Which feature is found by solving f(x)=0?
{
= x-intercept#Correct. An x-intercept occurs where the output is 0.
~ y-intercept#The y-intercept is found at x=0.
~ average rate of change#That compares output changes over an interval.
~ domain restriction#That identifies allowed input values.
}

